  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> be a triangle whose circumcentre is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. If the position vectors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> respectively, then the position vector of the orthocentre of this triangle, is :&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xZYz4",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
